.TH "DOCUMENTPICTUREINPICTURE" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DocumentPictureInPicture \- DocumentPictureInPicture
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]DocumentPictureInPicture\f[B]\f[R] interface of the
Document Picture\-in\-Picture API is the entry point for creating and
handling document picture\-in\-picture windows.
.PP
It is accessed via the \f[CR]Window.documentPictureInPicture\f[R]
property.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Inherits properties from its parent, \f[CI]EventTarget\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]window\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Window\f[R] instance representing the browsing context
inside the Picture\-in\-Picture window.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Inherits methods from its parent, \f[CI]EventTarget\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]requestWindow()\f[R]
Opens the Picture\-in\-Picture window for the current main browsing
context.
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that fulfills with a \f[CR]Window\f[R]
instance representing the browsing context inside the
Picture\-in\-Picture window.
.SH EVENTS
\f[I]Inherits events from its parent, \f[CI]EventTarget\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]enter\f[R]
Fired when the Picture\-in\-Picture window is successfully opened.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] videoPlayer = document.getElementById(\(dqplayer\(dq);

\f[I]// \&...\f[R]

\f[I]// Open a Picture\-in\-Picture window.\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] pipWindow = \f[B]await\f[R] window.documentPictureInPicture.requestWindow({
  width: videoPlayer.clientWidth,
  height: videoPlayer.clientHeight,
});

\f[I]// \&...\f[R]
.EE
.PP
See \c
.UR https://mdn.github.io/dom-examples/document-picture-in-picture/
Document Picture\-in\-Picture API Example
.UE \c
\ for a full working demo (see the full \c
